>>>>> "Aloysius" == Aloysius Kinsella <aloysius@cs.uiuc.edu> writes:

Aloysius> Weapon proficencies.  Not by selecting type, but by each
Aloysius> individual weapon.  as a character wields a weapon longer,
Aloysius> their tohit SLOWLY goes up.  

I actually wrote a patch for NetHack to do this.  

Or rather, I added a `knowledge' field to each object type.  Each time
you used the object, your knowledge of it would increase.  The only
thing that was implemented was automatically identifying various
aspects of the objects, as your knowledge of them reached certain
levels, but the intention was to make you better at using the objects
as you trained with them.

Some ideas for how knowledge may help:

weapons: tohit or todam.
armour: dexterity.
wands: precision or power of bolts.
scrolls: spells.

I did mail the patch to the dev-team, but never got a response, so I
assume they did not like it.


